<style>
    body {
        font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
        margin: 0;
        background-image: url(<%= image_path('backgroundaboutus.jpg') %>);
        background-position: center;
        background-attachment: fixed;
    }

    html {
        box-sizing: border-box;
    }

    *,
    *:before,
    *:after {
        box-sizing: inherit;
    }

    .column {
        float: left;
        width: 50%;
        margin-bottom: 16px;
        padding: 0 8px;
    }

    .card {
        box-shadow: 0 4px 8px 0 rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.2);
        margin: 8px;
        background: white;
    }

    .about-section {
        padding: 50px;
        text-align: center;
        background: #474e5d;
        border-radius: 50px;

        width: 1000px;
        margin: auto;
        margin-top: 50px;
        color: white;
    }

    .about-section h1 {
        font-size: 2.5rem;
        margin: 0 0 16px;
        text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    .container {
        padding: 0 16px;
    }

    .container p {
        font-size: 0.95rem;
        line-height: 1.5;
        color: #555;
        margin: 8px 0;
    }

    .container::after,
    .row::after {
        content: "";
        clear: both;
        display: table;
    }

    .title {
        color: grey;
    }

    .team-title {
        width: 25rem;
        margin: 40px auto 16px;
        text-align: center;
        font-size: 1.75rem;
        color: #a0c9ff;
        text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    .button {
        margin-top: 30px;

        border: none;
        outline: 0;
        display: inline-block;
        padding: 8px;
        color: white;
        background-color: #000;
        text-align: center;
        cursor: pointer;
        width: 100%;
    }

    .button:hover {
        background-color: #555;
    }

    @media screen and (max-width: 650px) {
        .column {
            width: 100%;
            display: block;
        }
    }

    .card img {
        width: 150px;
        height: 300px;
        object-fit: cover;
        display: block;
        margin: 0 auto;
        border-radius: 8px;
        margin-bottom: 10px;
    }

    a {
        text-decoration: none;
        color: inherit;
    }

    .row .team-title {
        clear: both;
    }

    .about-description {
        padding-left: 100px;
        padding-right: 100px;
    }

    .cards {
        background: #ffffff07;
        width: fit-content;
        border-radius: 8px;
    }
</style>

<div class="about-section">
    <h1>About Us</h1>
    <p class="about-description">Pseudocoder is a web application created by Dharma and Miguel, who are ATCS students at BCA, as a mid-year project, designed to help everyone better understand their programs logic. Our program allows users to convert code from languages such as Java, and JavaScript into clear, human-readable pseudocode. By breaking down complex syntax into structured English explanations, it makes programming more approachable for beginners, learners, and anyone curious about how their presumbably "ai" generated code works.

        <br><br>The application is built using Ruby on Rails, utlizing the framework’s Model–View–Controller (MVC) style to provide a reliable and efficient user experience. Users can create accounts, securely log in with bcrypt, update their profiles, and manage their history. Passwords are encrypted with bcrypt, and token-based databases are implemented for password resets and email changes, ensuring both account security with hashing and reliance.

        <br><br> At the core of our Pseudocoder is a custom, hard coded Ruby parser-compilor-generator engine that handles all the heavy lifting (Miguel's so strong). Submitted code is first analyzed to detect its programming language by comparing it with the languages tokens, then it is tokenized into structured parts, parsed into an Abstract Syntax Tree (AST), and finally transformed into readable pseudocode through our generator. This system allows users to see exactly how their code executes in a readable and clean way, making programming concepts easier to understand.

        <br><br>Beyond its technicality and complex structures, our Pseudocoder also serves as a learning place. Users can view the output of previously compiled files, track their progress, and loopup their code changes anytime. This project reflects our dedication as BCA students to combining strong programming and logical skills with web development, creating a tool that only looks good but works to help others by acheiving real world results.
    </p>
</div>
